to electric vehicles, which reduces the number of jobs. Now, in Britain, I=
=E2=80=99m watching the same people who once campaigned for Brexit campaign=
 against renewables, which they say have raised energy bills. (There=E2=80=
=99s something to that; read on.)</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25=
px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Across the West, the cli=
mate has become another battleground in the culture wars. That=E2=80=99s on=
e reason why, despite an alarming list of deadly climate disasters around t=
he world, you don=E2=80=99t hear as many politicians talk about the climate=
 anymore. But that doesn=E2=80=99t mean they=E2=80=99re not thinking about =
it. Today I write about the politics driving a climate change rebrand.</spa=
n></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0=
